Z||000000||bHooper||10-20-2001||06:02 PM||||We met in Cary (near Raleigh). And even thought there were only 8 of us, we had a good time.<P>Everyone was able to drool over Bert's freshly painted '86 SE 3.4 liter.  The last time we saw this car, Ed was delivering it after doing the install.  This car looked like a complete wreck, but now looks shiney and new!  When Ed delivered this car, he picked up a GT from Bert and is installing a 4.9 liter into it!<P>We had a demonstration on how to brake into a fiero, as Gary (Flyntus) locked his keys in his car and we had to open the thing with a coat hanger.  This is a very nice modification, and I suggest that we all cary coat hangers in our trunk, in case we lock our keys in the car!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>One fella even came from Myrtle Beach <B>(I believe that Myrtle Beach, South Carolina is further away than Hamlet, NC)</B>, I think his name was Richard.  He has a couple of fiero's and is going to do a Quad 4 swap into one.<P>All for now.<P><BR>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u><p>[This message has been edited by bHooper (edited 10-20-2001).]||||reg||6
